-- title:
--   Unit germ at a crossing from unit values on the tube
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero level $M$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$, and the hypothesis $hj$ that `jqModC` over $\mathbb{Q}$ lies in the $q$-expansion function field of the full level; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, with its integral, proper, flat model over $R_p$, its curve model `Meta` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with function field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` and the isomorphism `eeta` onto the base change. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit, with algebraically closed residue field of characteristic $p$, and $\rho : R_p \to A$ compatible with the structure map; let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, with $\rho_O : R_p \to O$, a surjective $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa_A$ compatible with $\rho$, an embedding $j_O : O \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $R_p$, and a lift $\iota_A : O \to A$ of $j_O$ inducing $\mathrm{to}\kappa$ on residue fields. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two components `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` and `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 1` of the special fibre, and let $x_n$ denote its image in the model $X_O$ over $O$ under the first projection, the component $0$ and `bcMap`. The crossing data consist of $e \ge 1$, an open $U \subseteq X_O$ containing $x_n$, and a morphism $f$ from $U$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `CrossingQuotient` $O$ at $p^e$, that is $O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1-p^e)$, subject to: $f$ is a morphism over $\operatorname{Spec} O$; the two coordinates both lie in the prime $f(y)$ exactly at the points of $U$ lying over $x_n$; at such points the stalk map of $f$ is flat, carries the maximal ideal onto the maximal ideal and induces an isomorphism of residue fields, and $f$ is étale on a neighbourhood; and membership of the second (respectively first) coordinate in $f(y)$ is equivalent to $y$ lying in the image of the component $0$ (respectively $1$) of the special fibre. Write $X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ for the base change of the model to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with the projections $\mathrm{pr}_J$ to $X_O$ induced by $j_O$ and $\mathrm{pr}_A$ to $X_A$ induced by the inclusion of $A$, and $\mathrm{bc}_A$ for the comparison of the special fibre with $X_A$. The assertion is that for every $g$ in `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` the following implication holds. Suppose that for every place $W$ of this function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field is generated by $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and every $A$-point $s$ of $U$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\iota_A$ whose restriction along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $X_O$ attached to $W$ by `Meta.pointEquivPlace` followed by `eeta` and $\mathrm{pr}_J$, and whose closed point maps to $x_n$, one has $\operatorname{ord}_W g = 0$ and $W.\mathrm{evalAt}\, g$ lies in $A$ and is a unit there. Then there are an open $U'$ of $X_A$ containing the image of $n$ under the first projection, the component $0$ and $\mathrm{bc}_A$, with the generic point of `Meta.C` lying in the preimage of $U'$ under `eeta` followed by $\mathrm{pr}_A$, and a section $\gamma \in \Gamma(X_A, U')$ such that: $\gamma$ is a unit; the germ of the pullback of $\gamma$ at the generic point of `Meta.C`, read in the function field through `Meta.ffEquiv`, equals $g$; and, for the fibre curve model `𝔛.Mfib A hA ρ hρ` (integral), the generic point of its underlying curve lies in the preimages of $U'$ under `efib` followed by the component $1$ and $\mathrm{bc}_A$, respectively the component $0$ and $\mathrm{bc}_A$, the two corresponding readings of $\gamma$ in the function field of the fibre model are nonzero, and they have order $0$ at the places `𝔛.placeOn1 A hA ρ hρ n` and `𝔛.placeOn0 A hA ρ hρ n` respectively.
--
--   This is the unit principle for the tube of a crossing of the Deligne–Rapoport model: a function on $X_H(M)$ with neither zero nor pole and unit values at all rational places of the tube above a node is the reading of a unit section on a neighbourhood of the node in the model over $A$, whose restrictions to the two components through the node are nonzero of order zero at the node places. It is used in the computation of the width of the annulus attached to a crossing at both ends.
